      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "40b80bc0485c7c651c33f67586c5e24b0bff061b",
            "subject": "LU-20867 gss: re-resolve lsvcgssd ioctl device on failure"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 20:42:57.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-31 01:16:07.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: test one upgrade image per conf-sanity 32a-d",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: test one upgrade image per conf-sanity 32a-d\n\nEach of conf-sanity 32a, 32b, 32c and 32d runs t32_test over every\ndisk image tarball (five for ldiskfs, three for zfs), so the four\ntests together took about 1900 hours of CI time per 30 days, and\nthat grows as new version images are added.\n\nWith SLOW=no, test one image per subtest. 32a to 32d pass $SLOW to\nt32_check to opt in, and each such call takes the next image from\nthe version sorted list, starting at the build version (including\nthe commit count, e.g. 2.17.60.45), so 32a to 32d test four\nconsecutive images, and a repeated subtest moves on to the next\nimage. A retest of the same build tests the same images, so a real\nfailure is not hidden by a different selection, while successive\nbuilds rotate every image through every subtest. T32INDEX=N sets\nthe starting index, to test one chosen image even with SLOW=yes.\n\nSLOW=yes and T32IMAGE keep testing every image. 32e to 32j already\ntest only the one image their upgraded feature needs.\n\nOn a rocky9 VM with ldiskfs (5 images), ONLY=\"32a 32b 32c 32d\":\n  before (SLOW=yes): 322 + 573 + 621 + 337 = 1853s, and 2699s\n  after  (SLOW=no):  about 310 to 460s over four runs\n\nRainshadow shows the four tests at a mean of 1641s per run over\nabout 4200 runs per 30 days. Saving about 1200s per run, about\n1300 hours per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=\"32a 32b 32c 32d\"\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ide3259cfbf5654070ba4cc94409e73c1485f7eb0\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
